-- title:
--   Base change of the full divisor-expansion field equals L(j,j_M)
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure and let $M$ be a nonzero natural number. Assume `FunctionFieldGeneration M`, i.e. for every nonzero divisor $d$ of $M$ the series $q \mapsto$ `qExpand ℚ d jq` (the Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ obtained from `jq` by the substitution $q \mapsto q^{d}$, formally the rescaling of the Hahn-series support by multiplication by $d$) lies in the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by `jq` and `qExpand ℚ M jq`. Then the base change to $L$ of `modularFunctionFieldFull M`, namely the intermediate field of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the subfield $\mathbb{Q}(\{\,$`qExpand ℚ d jq` $: d \mid M,\ d \neq 0\})$ of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$, coincides with the intermediate field of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the two elements `jqModC L` $= q^{-1}\cdot$ (image in $L$ of the integral power series $E_4^{3}\cdot$`dedekindEtaUnitInv`), the $q$-expansion of $j$ with coefficients in $L$, and `jqNModC L M` $=$ `qExpand L M (jqModC L)`, its substitution $q \mapsto q^{M}$.
--
--   This is the statement that the function field of $X_0(M)$ over a field $L$ of characteristic zero, modelled as a subfield of $L((q))$ spanned by all divisor expansions $j(q^{d})$ with $d \mid M$, is generated by the two functions $j(q)$ and $j(q^{M})$, once generation is known over $\mathbb{Q}$. It supplies the two-generator description of the base-changed function field used throughout the later analysis of places, nodes and specialisations of the $q$-expansion model of $X_0(M)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_laurentBaseChange_adjoin_pair.lean

